{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun13/packet-2.json'","aggregated_output":"[\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities approve imports of Nvidia H200 chips by Chinese firms by 2027-01-31, as shown by official Chinese government decisions or announcements?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: On or before 2027-01-31 Chinese authorities have officially approved imports of H200 chips by at least one Chinese firm.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: An official Chinese refusal of the requests to import H200 chips, or a prohibition of the imports, issued after 2026-07-08, stands on 2027-01-31 with no firm approved. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-08, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 1,\n    \"facts\": \"Alibaba received an official approval in October 2026 for a limited quantity; ByteDance was refused in November.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 2,\n    \"facts\": \"ByteDance withdrew its request in September 2026. The requests of Alibaba and DeepSeek are still under review on the due day. No firm has been approved.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 3,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 the authorities refused every request and announced that no H200 imports will be approved. Nothing has changed since.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 4,\n    \"facts\": \"In December 2026 every firm withdrew its request after a rule required domestic chips. No request is left, and no firm was approved.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 5,\n    \"facts\": \"Alibaba received an official approval in October 2026. The approval was revoked in December 2026.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 6,\n    \"facts\": \"There has been no official announcement of any kind. Press reports say requests were filed in July 2026. No firm has been approved.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 7,\n    \"facts\": \"The restriction on H200 imports that China had in place before July 2026 is unchanged on the due day. There has been no new decision, and no firm has been approved.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will the US Commerce Department adopt a binding restriction, a licensing rule or any other, on advanced AI-chip shipments to third countries beyond its May 2026 guidance by 2027-01-31, as shown by a Federal Register rule or a formal export-control action?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: On or before 2027-01-31 the Commerce Department has adopted a binding restriction, a licensing rule or any other, on advanced AI-chip shipments to third countries beyond its May 2026 guidance.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: An announcement by the Commerce Department, made after 2026-07-14, that it will adopt no such restriction stands on 2027-01-31. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-14, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 8,\n    \"facts\": \"A licensing rule for AI-chip shipments to third countries was published in the Federal Register in November 2026, and further firms were added to the entity list in December.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 9,\n    \"facts\": \"A proposed rule was withdrawn in October 2026. Another proposed rule, issued in December, is open for comment on the due day. No restriction has been adopted.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 10,\n    \"facts\": \"In November 2026 the Commerce Department announced that it will not go beyond the May guidance and withdrew its only proposal. Nothing has changed since.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 11,\n    \"facts\": \"A binding licensing rule was adopted in September 2026 and rescinded on 2027-01-15.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 12,\n    \"facts\": \"There has been no proposal and no announcement. The May 2026 guidance is as it was.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 13,\n    \"facts\": \"Export restrictions adopted in 2025, before the May 2026 guidance, are still in force. Nothing has been adopted or announced since the guidance.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia make H200 sales to customers in China by 2027-01-31, as shown by Nvidia's disclosures or by official Chinese statements published on or before that day?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: On or before 2027-01-31 Nvidia has made H200 sales to customers in China, as shown by Nvidia's disclosures or by official Chinese statements published on or before that day.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: A formal Chinese prohibition on purchases of H200 chips by Chinese customers, imposed after 2026-07-02, stands on 2027-01-31. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-07-02, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2027-01-31, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2027-01-31.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 14,\n    \"facts\": \"Beijing prohibited purchases in August 2026 and lifted the prohibition in December. No sale has been shown by the due day.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 15,\n    \"facts\": \"Beijing prohibited purchases in August 2026. The prohibition is in force on the due day; a review of it was announced in January 2027. No sale has been made.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 16,\n    \"facts\": \"Nvidia's Form 10-Q published in November 2026 discloses revenue from H200 sales to a Chinese customer.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 17,\n    \"facts\": \"Beijing announced in September 2026 that purchases are permitted. No sale has been disclosed or shown by the due day.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 18,\n    \"facts\": \"The bar on purchases that Beijing had in place in June 2026 has simply continued. There has been no new decision of any kind, and no sale.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"question\": \"Will Nvidia complete its announced acquisition of Hugging Face by 2028-03-05, as reported in Nvidia's Form 8-K, Form 10-Q or Form 10-K?\",\n  \"due_day\": \"2028-03-05\",\n  \"rungs\": [\n   \"rung 1 Yes: Nvidia has completed the acquisition of Hugging Face on or before 2028-03-05.\",\n   \"rung 2 Ruled out: A termination of the acquisition announced by Nvidia or Hugging Face after 2026-09-05, or a regulator's block of it after that day, stands on 2028-03-05. This rung holds when that, or any other decision against the event of rung 1 as a whole taken after 2026-09-05, or a formal abandonment or withdrawal of it as a whole after that day, stands on 2028-03-05, and only when rung 1 does not.\",\n   \"rung 3 Still open: Neither rung 1 nor rung 2 holds on 2028-03-05.\"\n  ],\n  \"facts_on_the_due_day\": [\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 19,\n    \"facts\": \"The acquisition closed in June 2027 at a renegotiated price of $11.0 billion.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 20,\n    \"facts\": \"The merger agreement expired in January 2028 and both companies confirmed that they will not go on with the deal.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 21,\n    \"facts\": \"A US regulator sued to block the deal in 2027. The case is still in court on the due day. The deal has not closed, and neither company has ended it.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 22,\n    \"facts\": \"A court blocked the deal in December 2027. Nvidia has appealed, and the appeal is pending on the due day.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"scenario\": 23,\n    \"facts\": \"The deal has not closed. Neither company has announced anything except that the latest date for closing was moved to September 2028.\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
